<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's Bucaram to address nation at 1800 GMT.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's Bucaram to address nation at 1800 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO, Ecuador 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's embattled President Abdala Bucaram will address the nation at 1300 local (1800 GMT) about the social unrest rocking the country, presidential sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Earlier on Thursday unions began the second day of a 48-hour general strike against tough austerity measures and Congress was due to meet at 1800 local (2300 GMT), amid speculation that legislators might try to dismiss Bucaram.</p>
